SF Unlimited Flight is a standalone ShroudForge runtime mod. Its package ID is <code>sf-unlimited-flight</code>. It targets the client and Dedicated Server, has no dependency on SF Survival, and is disabled by default. When enabled, Upward Gliding and Unlimited Glider Stamina start on. The four percentage multipliers start at 100%.

{| class="wikitable"
! Setting !! Default when enabled !! Range and effect
|-
| Upward Gliding || On || Steers each gliding player independently, including upward pitch.
|-
| Unlimited Glider Stamina || On || Sets the active glider's stamina-depletion modifier to zero.
|-
| Turn Speed || 100% || 25–400% in steps of 5. Multiplies the original glider yaw rate.
|-
| Move Speed || 100% || 25–400% in steps of 5. Multiplies the original forward acceleration.
|-
| Lift Speed || 100% || 25–400% in steps of 5. Multiplies longitudinal air resistance. Higher values add drag.
|-
| Descend Speed || 100% || 25–400% in steps of 5. Multiplies vertical air resistance. Higher values add drag.
|}

== Steering ==

Run the mod in the process that owns the world: the host for a hosted world or the Dedicated Server for a dedicated world. A joined client with read-only replica access cannot steer server entities. There is no player-count limit in the mod.

The mod samples steering input and landing every 100 milliseconds. In pitch-speed mode, it integrates each player's input using the original glider pitch rate. Negative input climbs, neutral input holds, and positive input descends. In target-angle mode, it steers toward the player's input multiplied by 90 degrees, using the same original rate. Individual movement steps stop at 85 degrees upward and 80 degrees downward. An inverted player recovers toward that player's own target angle.

The game's original systems continue to calculate yaw, bank, and forward movement. The four percentage settings multiply the active glider's original yaw, acceleration, and air-resistance values. Those values are shared by every player using the same glider resource, so multiplier changes can affect all of them.

== Multiplayer ownership and restoration ==

Each player's pitch is written to that player's own actor orientation target. The mod does not write the tracked <code>CurrentTransform</code> field. While steering, it temporarily sets a shared native pitch rate to zero so that the engine does not apply one player's steering sign to everyone sharing the resource.

All active users of a glider resource must be admitted before the shared rate is held. If an input mode is unsupported, the original rate is restored. The mod also restores it when the final active glider user lands, when the setting is disabled, and on unload. It does not rotate a player's current orientation back to an earlier pose.

Disable shared settings before leaving the world and wait for restoration. The loader performs cleanup when the mod is disabled, unloaded, or its callback fails. The current package README reports fixture coverage for opposing inputs, recovery, write failures, and restoration. Those fixtures do not prove visible multiplayer movement. A live client-and-server flight check is still required for that.

